<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baltic Germans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Baltic Germans were the German-speaking nobles, clergy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> and Latvia, descended mainly from settlers who came with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusades</a> of the 13th century. They kept their privileges and owned most of the land under Swedish and then Russian rule. Land reforms in independent Estonia and Latvia after 1919 broke their estates, and most were resettled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1939.</p></div>
